>Hey,

>Also I have a couple of speicific questions:
>1) I have no scrolls of gold detection, OR any ways of getting confused. So
>from the spoilers I have read this could be a problem for locating portals
>in the planes. I remember seeing a crystal ball earlier in the game, is it
>important that I go and find it to help me in this.

Getting  confused should be no problem. You're bound to have some spell
that you don't cast much (or at all). Let it lapse into asterixdom, and
then you can confuse yourself at will by attempting to cast that spell.
Doesn't even use any spellpoints.

>2) I've read about putting my BoH and unicorn horn inisde another bag incase
>they get cursed. But don't bags in bags explode? Also, will this mean I
>have to take the BoH out of the bag everytime I want something, slowing me
>down?

Never put your unihorn inside a bag. Bless it and keep it ready and
available. 

When people talk about putting stuff in a second bag, they mean in case
your BoH becomes cursed (which is bad). Make it an oilskin bag or a just a
normal sack, and put in a single vial of Holy Water, and possibly your
wands of cancellation (to keep them from endangering your BoH). If your BoH
gets cursed, take the water out of the second bag, uncurse the BoH, then
pull 2 holy waters out of your BoH, re-bless your BoH, and put the spare in
the second bag.

>4) Do I need more than one lamp? I have a few spare I could take, but then
>I'd be carrying even more stuff.

If it is magic, then no. If they are not magic, then I'd also say
no....having to fiddle around with lamps is simply not worth the hassle.
Use lightspells, or wands/scrolls of light.

>5) Finally, 

